--TEST--
`Core\Response\Stream::write` past the length the stream was started with throws a `LogicError` and sends nothing -- `rule:http-server/static-serving-is-one-policy`
--FILE--
<?nvs
var $stream = Core\Response::stream("text/plain", 3);
$stream->write("abc");
try {
    $stream->write("d");
} catch (LogicError $past) {
    echo "\n", $past->message, "\n";
}
// The refused part was not counted, so the window is still full.
echo $stream->offset(), " ", $stream->length(), "\n";
--EXPECT--
abc
Core\Response\Stream::write(): this part is 1 bytes, and only 0 bytes of the stream's length are left. Nothing was sent.
0 3
